# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A macro name carries the characters the host's own name regexp admits"

# TiddlyWiki reads a macro name with /([^\s>"'=:]+)/y — parseMacroInvocationAsTransclusion
# in core/modules/parsers/parseutils.js. Colon, quote and equals END the name, and a name
# of zero characters fails the call outright.
#
# Every negative below stands beside a positive at the same column, so a column that stopped
# naming anything fails loudly rather than passing empty. Every column here comes off a
# snapshot of these same lines, never off a hand count.

! A name of ordinary letters reads to its end

x <<myMacro>> y
# ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.macrocallinline.begin.tiddlywiki5
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#         ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#          ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.macrocallinline.end.tiddlywiki5

! A colon ends the name, and what follows it reads as a parameter

x <<a:b>> y
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ - variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macro.parameters.tiddlywiki5

! An equals sign ends the name the same way

x <<a=b>> y
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ - variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5 meta.variable.macro.parameters.tiddlywiki5

! A call carrying no name at all opens nothing

# The fr-FR edition writes this as prose about camel case, and TiddlyWiki builds plain text
# from it. No macro call stands here — and because the parser refuses the markup rather than
# reading it, the brackets fall back to the prose around them and carry no verdict.
NDT<<:>> here
#  ^ - punctuation.definition.macrocallinline.begin.tiddlywiki5
#  ^ - meta.variable.macrocallinline.tiddlywiki5
#  ^ - invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ - variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#    ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5

